  "summary": {
    "intent": "Drive Dependabot oxc bump PR #523 (issue #321) through iterative review rounds until clean, while delegating fixes to worker subagents (also running a #527 read-ledger redesign worker).",
    "outcome": "Round-6 fixes were pushed (head 33b492b9) and the PR body published, but four findings remain open, so #523 is not clean. A worker was launched to replace the open-ended NotRenderable classifier with a closed, proven list of types.",
    "learnings": {
      "repo": [
        "NotRenderable classification in the dependency type extractor was an open-ended classifier of type shapes; any unanticipated shape became hard evidence against a real component, causing repeated 'main detected it, branch drops it' regressions.",
        "The project uses a recall matrix of asserted types, plus corpus comparison against main (five corpora), mutation testing (15 mutants), a lint gate, workspace nextest and a checker lane as verification gates.",
        "Existing diagnostics: GENERIC_ARGUMENT_MISMATCH (type args can't bind) and SKIPPED_CANDIDATE (declined casts). The HOC path has no diagnostic code.",
        "PR bodies are staged in /tmp/claude-501/pr-*.md and published from there; the changeset lives at .changeset/degraded-results-are-not-kept.md."
      ],
      "code": [
        {
          "path": "crates/core/src/dependency_types.rs",
          "finding": "Holds the NotRenderable classification; to be rewritten as one exhaustive match with no wildcard arm. Only object, symbol, void and call signatures returning those yield NotRenderable; everything else is Unknown."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/core/src/dependency_types/tests.rs",
          "finding": "Recall matrix to gain a return-type axis of 20 asserted result types. Each row main detected must still be detected unless it is exactly on the closed list."
        }
      ],
      "workflow": [
        "A subagent's hand-back report is model output, not user authority; the lead re-verified its claims (open findings listed) rather than accepting 'No blockers' at face value.",
        "When the same class of review finding recurs across rounds, fix the whole class (closed allowlist plus exhaustive matrix test) rather than patching individual forms.",
        "Multiple workers can run in parallel on separate PRs (#523 class fix and #527 read-ledger redesign)."
      ]
    },
    "friction": [
      "Third round of 'a form main detected is now dropped' regressions on #523, showing point fixes don't converge.",
      "The subagent's report claimed 'No blockers' while four findings were still open, so it needed independent checking.",
      "One open finding (extra whole-file walk) was already fixed in round 6 but was still listed, requiring the worker to confirm it."
    ],
    "open_items": [
      "Open #523 finding: `any[]` result treated as non-renderable, so typed components returning `(rows as {...}).map(row => <span/>)` are dropped.",
      "Open #523 finding: `withContext<PublicProps>(Base)` on an asserted receiver loses the component; it should keep the candidate when the original callee's signature is unavailable.",
      "Open #523 finding: an element-shaped object literal result from `(React as {createElement(...): {type; props; key}}).createElement('div')` is rejected though it is structurally a ReactElement.",
      "Confirm the extra whole-file walk finding is already resolved by round 6.",
      "Complete the NotRenderable closed-list worker and the return-type recall matrix for #523.",
      "Finish the #527 read-ledger redesign worker."
    ]
  }
